        "original_id": "516c1768-01db-5d47-8f69-634625157eb9",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Species: Agonum fuliginosum\n- People: Panzer\n- Places: Europe, Albania, Andorra, Monaco, Portugal, San Marino, Vatican City, European islands\n- Organizations: Council of Europe\n\nFacts:\n- Panzer described Agonum fuliginosum in 1809.\n- Agonum fuliginosum can be found throughout Europe except in Albania, Andorra, Monaco, Portugal, San Marino, Vatican City, and various European islands.\n- San Marino has the smallest population among the members of the Council of Europe.",
